---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>The Flagship | Feels Like Om</title>
    <meta name="description" content="The Flagship — a small-group field immersion in West Sikkim with community learning, reflection and a 4D3N mountain trek." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/type-system.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Feels Like Om</a>
      <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary>ABOUT</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/about/our-story">Our story</a>
            <a href="/about/getting-to-sikkim">Getting to Sikkim</a>
            <a href="/about/visa-and-permits">Visa and permits</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary class="active">JOURNEYS</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/journeys/the-flagship" aria-current="page">The Flagship</a>
            <a href="/journeys/how-to-embrace-suffering">To Be Free</a>
            <a href="/journeys#feels-like-home">Feels Like Home</a>
            <a href="/journeys#way-of-the-yaks">Way of the Yaks</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a href="/reflections">REFLECTIONS</a>
        <a href="/contact">CONTACT</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="The Flagship page sections">
      <a href="#intentions"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Intentions</span></a>
      <a href="#itinerary"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Itinerary</span></a>
      <a href="#accommodation"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Accommodation</span></a>
      <a href="#food"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Food</span></a>
      <a href="#trek"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Trek</span></a>
      <a href="#reflections"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Reflections</span></a>
      <a href="#faq"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">FAQ</span></a>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-image" role="img" aria-label="A person looking across the mountains of West Sikkim beneath a dramatic sky"></div>
        <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">West Sikkim | Field Immersion | 4D3N Trek</p>
          <h1>The Flagship</h1>
          <div class="hero-dates" aria-label="Upcoming Flagship dates">
            <p>Nov 22 - Dec 2, 2026</p>
            <p>Dec 22 - Jan 1, 2027</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button hero-cta" href="#faq">Enquire about The Flagship</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opening-quote" aria-label="Opening reflection">
        <blockquote>
          <span>&ldquo;We don&rsquo;t see things as they are;</span>
          <span>we see them as we are.&rdquo;</span>
          <cite>— Anaïs Nin</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </section>

      <section id="intentions" class="program-intro" aria-label="About the program">
        <div class="program-intro-inner">
          <div class="program-images" aria-label="Journey image placeholders">
            <div class="image-placeholder program-image program-image-large"><span>Community / place photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder program-image program-image-small"><span>Hands-on journey photograph</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="program-row program-row-left">Equal parts community immersion and time in the mountains. It was designed by looking at what tourists usually do in Sikkim and inviting people into life beyond the overcrowded tourist circuit.</p>
          <p class="program-row program-row-right">Ease yourself into how life is lived in Yuksom. The days are unhurried, but your hands are busy and your heart is full. Churn butter, forage in the forest, learn the art of bamboo weaving.</p>
          <p class="program-row program-row-center">Let your curiosities guide the way you interact with the land, the people, and yourself.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="community-quote" aria-label="Community introduction">
        <blockquote>Meet the community who fought against a commercial company from exploiting the land.</blockquote>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section story-section-place">
        <div class="story-media image-placeholder tall"><span>Yuksom / community photograph</span></div>
        <div class="story-copy">
          <h2>Where you’ll be</h2>
          <p>Yuksom, West Sikkim. Gateway to the Khangchendzonga mountain range. Home to a community whose values have been shaped by the mountains they call home.</p>
          <p>Learn from the farmers, craftspeople, neighbours, aunties and uncles you will meet during the journey.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section story-section-reflection">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <h2>Hold space for yourself</h2>
          <p>Reflection sharpens your awareness of your inner world. Don’t underestimate the power of collective energy that comes from being in a supportive environment (even for just 11 days).</p>
          <p>Allow yourself to be seen. Be heard.</p>
          <p>Reflection will be an ongoing part of your journey. There will be intentional time+space for you to notice what is happening around you and what is happening within you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="story-media image-placeholder tall"><span>Reflection / quiet moment photograph</span></div>
      </section>

      <section id="itinerary" class="section rhythm" aria-label="The Flagship itinerary">
        <div class="wide">
          <h2 class="itinerary-heading">What your days may look like</h2>
          <div class="days-grid">
            <article><span>Day 1</span><h3>Arrival & Welcome</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 2</span><h3>Knowing our roots</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 3</span><h3>Everything is related</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 4</span><h3>Soil biome is gut biome</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 5</span><h3>Wildcard / Free & easy day</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 6</span><h3>Start of trek</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 7</span><h3>Summit day</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 8</span><h3>Rest day</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 9</span><h3>Descend day</h3></article>
            <article><span>Day 10</span><h3>Nature therapy</h3></article>
            <article class="day-eleven"><span>Day 11</span><h3>Not Goodbye</h3><p class="day-detail">The equivalent of ‘goodbye’ in Nepali is <em>pheri bhetum</em> — may we meet again.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="accommodation" class="section accommodation-section">
        <h2 class="accommodation-heading">Where you will stay</h2>
        <div class="image-placeholder accommodation-portrait"><span>Ejam Residency portrait photograph</span></div>
        <div class="accommodation-body">
          <p>Ejam Residency is a three-storey home in Yuksom. The Ejam family lives on the second floor.</p>
          <p>You’ll know why I insist on putting Feels Like Om guests here.</p>
          <p>There are private bathrooms, hot showers, laundry (and WIFI) — but past guests speak much more fondly of conversations shared with the family in the kitchen, mornings on the lawn, afternoons in the library.</p>
          <p>One guest’s favourite morning ritual: taking huge mouthfuls of fresh air from the balcony.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="accommodation-gallery-section" aria-label="Ejam Residency image placeholders">
        <div class="accommodation-gallery">
          <div class="image-placeholder accommodation-landscape"><span>Ejam Residency photograph</span></div>
          <div class="image-placeholder accommodation-landscape"><span>Room / kitchen / lawn photograph</span></div>
          <div class="image-placeholder accommodation-landscape"><span>Balcony / garden photograph</span></div>
          <div class="image-placeholder accommodation-landscape"><span>Shared spaces photograph</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="food" class="section food-grid">
        <div class="image-stack">
          <div class="image-placeholder"><span>Breakfast photograph</span></div>
          <div class="image-placeholder"><span>Dinner / local food photograph</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="copy-block">
          <h2>Nourish your gut, nourish your soul</h2>
          <p>Breakfast is a grand affair.</p>
          <p>Buckwheat pancakes one morning, <em>alu puri</em> the next. The spread changes daily. There is always fresh fruit, hot tea and coffee.</p>
          <p class="pull">Dinner is omakase. Food you can't find in restaurants.</p>
          <p><em>Cowrie. Hand-rolled gnochhi-like dumplings in hot, savoury soup.</em></p>
          <p><em>Iskus ko munta. The first shoots of the chayote — a plant that keeps giving.</em></p>
          <p><em>Nettle soup. Fiddlehead ferns. Edible flowers.</em></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <figure class="trek-wide-image" aria-label="Mountain landscape at Bajre Dara">
        <img src="/bajre-top.jpg" alt="Open mountain landscape at Bajre Dara" />
      </figure>

      <section id="trek" class="section trek-overview" aria-labelledby="trek-overview-title">
        <div class="wide trek-overview-inner">
          <h2 id="trek-overview-title">Into the mountains</h2>

          <div class="trek-stats" aria-label="Trek overview statistics">
            <article class="trek-stat"><h3>Duration</h3><p>4 days trek<br />3 nights camping</p></article>
            <article class="trek-stat"><h3>Distance</h3><p>~6 km one way</p></article>
            <article class="trek-stat"><h3>Elevation gain</h3><p>~1,300 m over two days</p></article>
            <article class="trek-stat"><h3>Highest point</h3><p>3,340 m</p></article>
          </div>

          <div class="trek-copy">
            <p class="trek-lead">This is a quiet trail, and we hope to keep it this way.</p>
            <div class="trek-photo-row" aria-label="Trek photograph placeholders">
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
            </div>
            <p>A two-day climb, moving slowly through forest, bamboo and rhododendron before reaching the higher, more open landscape.</p>
            <p>The trek covers approximately <strong>6 km one way</strong>, with around <strong>1,300 m of elevation gain spread across two days</strong>. The first two sections are steeper, while the final stretch eases slightly as you approach the top.</p>
            <figure class="trek-chart" aria-label="Elevation profile from approximately 2,100 metres at the start to 3,340 metres at 6 kilometres">
              <div class="trek-chart-image-wrap">
                <img src="/trek-graph.png" alt="Elevation profile for the 6 kilometre one-way trek, climbing from approximately 2,100 metres to 3,340 metres." />
                <div class="trek-chart-day-cover" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <span class="trek-chart-day trek-chart-day-one" aria-hidden="true">DAY 1</span>
                <span class="trek-chart-day trek-chart-day-two" aria-hidden="true">DAY 2</span>
              </div>
            </figure>
            <p>This is not a technical trek, but it is physically demanding. Expect <strong>several hours of uphill walking each day</strong>, uneven forest trails, roots, mud and occasional rocky sections. Conditions can become slippery after rain. Generally, most people consider this a moderate to challenging trek.</p>
            <p>The terrain consists of forested mountain trail, with earth, roots, bamboo, rhododendron and steeper uphill sections. The trail becomes more open as you gain elevation.</p>
            <div class="trek-photo-row" aria-label="More trek photograph placeholders">
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
              <div class="trek-photo-placeholder"><span>Trek photograph</span></div>
            </div>
            <h3 class="trek-subheading">This trek may be for you if</h3>
            <p>You are comfortable walking uphill for several hours, enjoy being outdoors in changing weather, and do not mind uneven or muddy trails. You do not need technical climbing experience, but a reasonable level of fitness and willingness to move slowly and steadily are important.</p>
            <p>The pace is intentionally unhurried. There will be space to stop, rest and take in the landscape rather than treating the trail as something to conquer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="reflections" class="section reflections">
        <div class="wide">
          <h2>Reflections from past participants</h2>
          <div class="reflection-grid">
            <div class="image-placeholder square"><span>Participant photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder square"><span>Participant photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder square"><span>Participant photograph</span></div>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/reflections">Read more reflections →</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="faq" class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <div class="narrow">
          <h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-list">
            <details><summary>Who is this journey for?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><ul><li>You are curious about the world</li><li>You want to do more than sightseeing</li><li>You learn by doing, experiencing, and reflecting</li><li>You want to experience culture as a participant rather than a spectator</li></ul></div></details>
            <details><summary>Do I need to be an experienced trekker?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Prior hiking experience will help, but it isn’t strictly necessary. We take short breaks and move at a pace the group can sustain. A reasonable level of fitness and stamina is required. Technical climbing skills are not required, but good balance — especially while descending rocky terrain — is helpful.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>How comfortable is camping?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Your well-being is very important to us. We provide A-frame tents, four-inch mattresses, down sleeping bags, camping pillows, fleece blankets, hot water bags, a dining tent with tables and chairs, a toilet tent with a commode, and multi-course meals three times a day.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>What do I need to carry during the trek?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>You only need to carry a light daypack with your water bottle, snacks, and an extra layer. The dzos carry the rest, which is why we ask you to pack only what you genuinely need.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>How does altitude acclimatisation work?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>For first-timers to mountainous areas, it is normal to get breathless more quickly than usual when walking uphill or climbing stairs. The few days we spend in Yuksom before the trek should give your body enough time to gradually adjust before we start the trek.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>How big is the group?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The Flagship is designed for a small group of 2–6 people. We keep the group intentionally small so there is space for connection, reflection and meaningful time with the community.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>How do I get to Yuksom?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The nearest airport is Bagdogra Airport in West Bengal.</p><p>From there, the drive to Yuksom takes approximately six hours. We can help coordinate your transfer so you don’t have to arrange the journey on your own.</p><p>Before booking your flights, please speak with us.</p><p>We'll share recommended arrival and departure times so that your airport transfer and the drive can be planned comfortably.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/about/getting-to-sikkim"><strong>Read our guide to getting to Sikkim →</strong></a></p></div></details>
            <details><summary>Do I need a visa or permit?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Depending on your nationality, you may need an Indian visa as well as the relevant permits to enter Sikkim.</p><p>We will guide you through the process before your trip.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/about/visa-and-permits"><strong>Read about visas and permits →</strong></a></p></div></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="faq-cta"><a class="button" href="/contact">Enquire about The Flagship →</a></div>
      <section id="enquire" class="section enquire"><div class="narrow center"><h2>Other journeys</h2></div></section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const sectionNav = document.querySelector('.section-nav');
      const hero = document.querySelector('.hero');
      const updateSectionNav = () => {
        if (!sectionNav || !hero) return;
        const heroBottom = hero.getBoundingClientRect().bottom;
        sectionNav.classList.toggle('is-visible', heroBottom <= 0);
      };
      updateSectionNav();
      window.addEventListener('scroll', updateSectionNav, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', updateSectionNav);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing:border-box; }
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior:smooth; scroll-padding-top:2rem; }
  body { margin:0; font-family:var(--font-body); background:#f4efe5; color:#18301f; }
  h1,h2,h3,blockquote,.brand,.pull { font-family:var(--font-display); }
  p { line-height:1.7; }
  .site-header { position:absolute; top:0; left:0; right:0; z-index:5; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:2rem; padding:1.5rem 4%; color:white; }
  .brand { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; white-space:nowrap; }
  .main-nav { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1.5rem; letter-spacing:.08em; }
  .main-nav > a,.main-nav summary { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; cursor:pointer; }
  .main-nav .active { border-bottom:1px solid currentColor; }
  .nav-dropdown { position:relative; }
  .nav-dropdown summary { list-style:none; }
  .nav-dropdown summary::-webkit-details-marker { display:none; }
  .submenu { position:absolute; top:calc(100% + .65rem); right:0; min-width:13rem; width:max-content; padding:.7rem; background:rgba(244,239,229,.98); box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(8,20,12,.14); opacity:0; visibility:hidden; transform:translateY(-4px); transition:opacity 160ms ease,visibility 160ms ease,transform 160ms ease; z-index:30; }
  .submenu::before { content:""; position:absolute; top:-.75rem; left:0; right:0; height:.75rem; }
  @media (hover:hover) { .nav-dropdown:hover .submenu { opacity:1; visibility:visible; transform:translateY(0); } .nav-dropdown:not(:hover) .submenu { opacity:0; visibility:hidden; transform:translateY(-4px); } }
  .submenu a { display:block; padding:.65rem .75rem; color:#18301f; text-decoration:none; letter-spacing:0; }
  .submenu a:hover { background:rgba(24,48,31,.06); }

  .section-nav { position:fixed; top:50%; right:1.15rem; z-index:20; width:42px; padding:.4rem .25rem; display:grid; gap:.1rem; background:transparent; border:0; box-shadow:none; backdrop-filter:none; transform:translateY(-50%); overflow:hidden; opacity:0; visibility:hidden; pointer-events:none; transition:width 240ms ease,opacity 220ms ease,visibility 220ms ease; }
  .section-nav.is-visible { opacity:1; visibility:visible; pointer-events:auto; }
  .section-nav:hover,.section-nav:focus-within { width:190px; }
  .section-nav a { min-height:38px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:flex-end; gap:.75rem; color:#18301f; text-decoration:none; white-space:nowrap; padding:.35rem .3rem; text-shadow:0 1px 10px rgba(244,239,229,.7); }
  .section-nav-dot { order:2; flex:0 0 auto; width:8px; height:8px; border-radius:50%; background:#18301f; opacity:.78; box-shadow:0 0 0 2px rgba(244,239,229,.5); }
  .section-nav-label { order:1; flex:1 1 auto; opacity:0; transform:translateX(6px); text-align:right; font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:.78rem; transition:opacity 180ms ease,transform 180ms ease; }
  .section-nav:hover .section-nav-label,.section-nav:focus-within .section-nav-label { opacity:1; transform:translateX(0); }

  .hero { position:relative; width:100%; min-height:96svh; display:flex; align-items:flex-end; color:white; overflow:hidden; }
  .hero-image { position:absolute; inset:-1%; background-image:url('/flagship-hero.jpg'); background-size:cover; background-position:center; transform:scale(1.01); }
  .hero-overlay { position:absolute; inset:0; background:linear-gradient(0deg,rgba(7,18,11,.62),rgba(7,18,11,.04) 62%); }
  .hero-copy { position:relative; z-index:2; width:100%; padding:0 4% clamp(3.2rem,6vw,5.6rem); text-align:right; }
  .eyebrow { margin:0 0 .65rem; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .hero h1 { margin:0; line-height:.95; font-weight:400; }
  .hero-dates { margin:1.5rem 0 0 auto; display:grid; gap:.25rem; width:max-content; max-width:100%; }
  .hero-dates p { margin:0; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1.8vw,1.6rem); }
  .button { display:inline-block; padding:.9rem 1.2rem; border:1px solid currentColor; color:inherit; text-decoration:none; font-family:var(--font-display); }
  .hero-cta { margin-top:1.35rem; background:rgba(244,239,229,.06); backdrop-filter:blur(2px); }
  .hero-cta:hover { background:#f4efe5; color:#18301f; }

  .opening-quote { width:100%; padding:clamp(4rem,8vw,7rem) 4%; text-align:center; }
  .opening-quote blockquote { width:min(850px,90%); margin:0 auto; line-height:1.25; }
  .opening-quote blockquote span { display:block; }
  .opening-quote cite { display:block; margin-top:1.3rem; font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:.72em; font-style:normal; text-align:right; }
  .program-intro { background:#18301f; color:#f4efe5; padding:clamp(5rem,10vw,9rem) 4%; }
  .program-intro-inner { width:min(1200px,100%); margin:0 auto; display:grid; gap:clamp(4rem,8vw,7rem); }
  .program-images { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(230px,.6fr); gap:clamp(1rem,3vw,2.25rem); align-items:end; }
  .program-image { border-color:rgba(244,239,229,.18); color:rgba(244,239,229,.62); background:rgba(244,239,229,.07); }
  .program-image-large { min-height:clamp(360px,46vw,600px); }
  .program-image-small { min-height:clamp(240px,28vw,370px); margin-bottom:-2rem; }
  .program-row { margin:0; max-width:760px; }
  .program-row-left { justify-self:start; }
  .program-row-right { justify-self:end; text-align:right; }
  .program-row-center { justify-self:center; text-align:center; max-width:900px; }
  .community-quote { padding:clamp(5rem,9vw,8rem) 4%; text-align:center; }
  .community-quote blockquote { width:min(900px,100%); margin:0 auto; line-height:1.08; }
  .story-section { width:min(1200px,92%); margin:0 auto; padding:clamp(5rem,10vw,9rem) 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,7rem); align-items:center; }
  .story-copy h2 { margin:0 0 1.6rem; line-height:1.04; }
  .story-copy p { margin:0 0 1.2rem; }
  .story-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }

  .section { padding:clamp(5rem,10vw,9rem) 4%; }
  .narrow { width:min(780px,100%); margin:0 auto; }
  .wide { width:min(1200px,100%); margin:0 auto; }
  .section h2 { margin:0 0 1.6rem; line-height:1.04; }
  .section h3 { line-height:1.1; }
  .image-placeholder { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:260px; background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgba(24,48,31,.18),rgba(24,48,31,.05)); border:1px solid rgba(24,48,31,.14); color:rgba(24,48,31,.62); text-align:center; padding:1rem; }
  .tall { min-height:620px; }

  .rhythm { background:#18301f; color:#f4efe5; padding-top:clamp(5rem,9vw,8rem); }
  .itinerary-heading { margin:0 0 clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem)!important; color:inherit; }
  .days-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); border-top:1px solid rgba(244,239,229,.25); }
  .days-grid article { padding:2rem 1.3rem 2.4rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(244,239,229,.25); }
  .days-grid article:nth-child(3n+2),.days-grid article:nth-child(3n+3) { padding-left:1.3rem; border-left:1px solid rgba(244,239,229,.25); }
  .days-grid span { font-size:.72rem; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; opacity:.72; }
  .days-grid h3 { margin:.5rem 0 0; }
  .day-detail { margin:0; }

  .accommodation-section { width:min(1200px,92%); margin:0 auto; padding-left:0; padding-right:0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; grid-template-areas:"heading portrait" "body portrait"; column-gap:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,7rem); row-gap:1rem; align-items:start; }
  .accommodation-heading { grid-area:heading; margin:0!important; }
